WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.667 --> 00:00:20.362
One day John Manly and I rode out to deliver a message for the squire.

2
00:00:20.363 --> 00:00:26.478
On our way home, we saw a teenage boy riding a stout black pony.

3
00:00:26.479 --> 00:00:30.930
John and I watched as the boy rode the pony toward a gate near the road.

4
00:00:30.931 --> 00:00:36.566
On either side of the gate was a tall hedge.

5
00:00:36.567 --> 00:00:38.852
"Is he crazy?" John murmured.

6
00:00:38.853 --> 00:00:42.756
"That gate is much too high for a pony that size to jump."

7
00:00:42.757 --> 00:00:46.522
The pony seemed to be thinking the same thing.

8
00:00:46.523 --> 00:00:50.494
When he reached the gate, he veered off to the right and stopped.

9
00:00:50.495 --> 00:00:54.204
"Hey!" the boy shouted.

10
00:00:54.205 --> 00:00:58.325
He spun the pony around and tried again.

11
00:00:58.326 --> 00:01:06.337
This time he thumped the pony's sides with his heels and gave him several cracks with his whip.

12
00:01:06.338 --> 00:01:13.303
But once again the pony refused the jump. Instead he darted off to the left.

13
00:01:13.304 --> 00:01:17.333
"You rotten little thing!" the boy cried.

14
00:01:17.334 --> 00:01:21.168
He still didn't notice John and me watching.

15
00:01:21.169 --> 00:01:28.905
The boy wheeled the pony around and aimed him at the gate once again, kicking as hard as he could and lashing him with the whip.

16
00:01:28.906 --> 00:01:33.597
The pony's ears were flat back against his head.

17
00:01:33.598 --> 00:01:36.631
This time the pony turned neither left nor right.

18
00:01:36.632 --> 00:01:41.868
He just stopped short, threw his head down, and bucked several times.

19
00:01:41.869 --> 00:01:47.143
The boy tried to hang on. But the last buck sent him flying.

20
00:01:47.144 --> 00:01:52.210
He went right over the pony's shoulder, landing headfirst in the thorny hedge.

21
00:01:52.211 --> 00:01:59.246
"Ow!" he yelled, thrashing around. "Stupid thorns!"

22
00:01:59.247 --> 00:02:07.083
Meanwhile the pony spun around and galloped off, his reins dangling.

23
00:02:07.084 --> 00:02:12.160
John burst out laughing. "That boy got what he deserved," he said.

24
00:02:12.161 --> 00:02:16.508
The boy heard him. "Help!" he called.

25
00:02:16.509 --> 00:02:23.510
"Come help me out of these thorns so I can catch that rotten pony and teach him a lesson!"

26
00:02:23.511 --> 00:02:27.705
"I think you're the one who needs the lesson, young man," John said.

27
00:02:27.706 --> 00:02:30.742
"And those thorns seem to be giving you one.

28
00:02:30.743 --> 00:02:36.337
Maybe next time you'll know better than to try to make your pony jump over such a high gate.

29
00:02:36.338 --> 00:02:40.104
Or to use the whip so cruelly."

30
00:02:40.105 --> 00:02:46.851
We rode off, with the boy's cries following us part of the way.

31
00:02:46.852 --> 00:02:50.830
When we reached the next intersection, John turned off to the right.

32
00:02:50.831 --> 00:02:55.100
"I think we'd better stop by Farmer Bushby's house, Beauty," he said.

33
00:02:55.101 --> 00:02:59.041
"That young man might be a liar as well as a bad rider.

34
00:02:59.042 --> 00:03:05.855
It might be better for that pony if we're there to tell his side of the story."

35
00:03:05.856 --> 00:03:08.404
We rode up to a farmhouse.

36
00:03:08.405 --> 00:03:13.063
A man was standing in the road looking back and forth with a worried expression.

37
00:03:13.064 --> 00:03:16.938
His wife was nearby, and she looked frightened too.

38
00:03:16.939 --> 00:03:19.767
The black pony was grazing in the yard.

39
00:03:19.768 --> 00:03:25.165
He was still wearing his saddle, but he looked much more content without his rider.

40
00:03:25.166 --> 00:03:29.827
"Hello, Mr. Manly," the farmer said when he saw us.

41
00:03:29.828 --> 00:03:35.674
"Have you seen my boy anywhere? His pony just came home without him."

42
00:03:35.675 --> 00:03:39.091
"As a matter of fact, I have," John replied.

43
00:03:39.092 --> 00:03:44.049
"And after seeing the way he rides, his pony is better off without him."

44
00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:47.788
"What do you mean?" the farmer asked.

45
00:03:47.789 --> 00:03:54.350
"Well, sir, I saw your son whipping and kicking that good-looking pony to make him jump," John said.

46
00:03:54.351 --> 00:03:59.803
"But the pony knew better than to try to make it over a gate that was far too high for him.

47
00:03:59.804 --> 00:04:04.608
He finally kicked up his heels and tipped the young man into a thorn hedge.

48
00:04:04.609 --> 00:04:07.509
Your son wanted me to help him out.

49
00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:15.143
But I could tell that the boy had no injuries aside from the scratches the thorns were giving him, and so I decided to leave him where he was.

50
00:04:15.144 --> 00:04:19.422
I love horses, and it bothers me to see them treated badly."

51
00:04:19.423 --> 00:04:25.769
The farmer's wife was crying by now. "Oh, poor Bill!" she sobbed.

52
00:04:25.770 --> 00:04:29.158
"We should go find him and help him."

53
00:04:29.159 --> 00:04:34.291
"I think I'd better go by myself, my dear," the farmer said with a sigh.

54
00:04:34.292 --> 00:04:39.464
"This is not the first time Bill has mistreated that pony, or the second either.

55
00:04:39.465 --> 00:04:45.791
It's time to put a stop to it and teach him a lesson." He nodded toward John.

56
00:04:45.792 --> 00:04:49.671
"Thank you for letting us know about this, Mr. Manly."

57
00:04:49.672 --> 00:04:54.743
"You're welcome," John said. "Good luck with your boy."

58
00:04:54.744 --> 00:04:59.263
When we got home, James was there to remove my saddle and groom me.

59
00:04:59.264 --> 00:05:02.544
While they worked, John told him what had happened.

60
00:05:02.545 --> 00:05:05.991
Soon the two of them were both chuckling.

61
00:05:05.992 --> 00:05:09.697
"I know the boy you mean," James said.

62
00:05:09.698 --> 00:05:12.586
"And you were right about his needing that lesson.

63
00:05:12.587 --> 00:05:16.057
He's always been careless about animals.

64
00:05:16.058 --> 00:05:19.173
Maybe this will teach him to treat them better."

65
00:05:19.174 --> 00:05:25.423
"I hope so," John replied. "Only a coward is cruel to helpless animals.

66
00:05:25.424 --> 00:05:28.306
At least this coward is still only a boy.

67
00:05:28.307 --> 00:05:34.991
If his father can get him to change his ways, there may be hope for him yet."
